---
import Layout from "@components/Layout.astro";
import PageHeader from "@components/PageHeader.astro";
import { Card } from "webcoreui/astro";
---

<Layout
    title="Conclusion & Credits - Replenish Guide | Premodern MTG"
    image="/src/assets/banners/abeyance.webp"
    description="Reflections on the Premodern Magic community and shoutouts to the players who helped shape this Replenish guide."
>
    <PageHeader
        title="Conclusion & Credits"
        description="A few final thoughts on what makes Premodern special, and huge thanks to the community members who helped elevate this archetype."
        imageSrc="/src/assets/banners/abeyance.webp"
        imageAlt="Abeyance"
        imageCaption="Abeyance by Thomas Gianni"
        isCard={true}
    />

    <Card title="The Spirit of the Gathering" titleTag="h2">
        <p
            class="text-body"
        >
            At the end of the day, all the stack mechanics, matchup percentages,
            and sideboard guides serve one simple purpose: <strong
                class="text-highlight"
                >playing a game we love with people we respect.</strong
            >
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 0; color: var(--w-color-primary-20);">
            Premodern is special precisely because the human connection comes
            first. When we sit down across the table—whether in a massive
            regional tournament or at a kitchen table with a beer—the ultimate
            victory isn't locking an opponent out of the game; it's the shared
            laughs, the appreciation for classic old-frame cards, and the chats
            between rounds. Play hard, play with precision, but always remember
            that the greatest magic is the gathering itself.
        </p>
    </Card>

    <Card title="Acknowledgments & Credits" titleTag="h2">
        <p
            class="text-body"
        >
            This guide is the result of years of tournament playtesting, endless
            Discord debates, and refinement by the Premodern community. A
            massive thank you to the following players who made this possible:
        </p>
        <ul
            style="padding-left: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.75rem;"
        >
            <li>
                <strong>Brian Siu (Dr Siuss):</strong> Author of the original Premodern
                Replenish primer that inspired the creation of this guide.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Gary Roth:</strong> The rules guru behind the definitive explanation
                of the Parallax Wave and Opalescence interactions.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>The Premodern Replenish Discord Community:</strong> The entire
                group of players testing, debating, and pushing the archetype forward
                every day. Special thanks to
                <strong>The Atog Lord</strong>, <strong>justint</strong>, <strong
                    >Pylse</strong
                >,
                <strong>Rich_Card_O</strong>, <strong>Eichhorn (Ben V)</strong>,
                <strong>aardshark (galen)</strong>, <strong
                    >Marine Biomancer</strong
                >,
                <strong>Bitner</strong>, <strong>chowder</strong>, <strong
                    >Lannynyny</strong
                >,<strong>Coinman</strong> and <strong> jcl </strong> for their invaluable
                insights.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </Card>
</Layout>
